BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sjn": "https://uri-edu.zoom.us/meeting/register/5BFu_GsqT3qDJjYz_ijy0g"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sjn
SUMMARY:Covering the Planet with the Tools That Tax It: AI for Climate\, S
 cience and Environmental Journalists
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T000000
UID:3cc7ebffa03e25798c7ec36852a0625e@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Online\nAI is both a tool transforming newsrooms and a story-s
 haping force in public life. How should journalists approach both with rig
 or?\nJoin us for a one-hour session with journalist and SF State Universit
 y Professor Yumi Wilson. We'll talk about AI using the solutions journalis
 m framework. We'll examine what AI actually does in newsrooms (response)\,
  what the evidence shows about its costs and benefits (evidence)\, what re
 porters are learning about its best uses (insight) and where AI falls shor
 t (limitations). You'll come away with a clearer understanding of how AI i
 s shaping journalism worldwide and a practical prompting structure you can
  start using on the beat.
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://uri-edu.zoom.us/meeting/register/5BFu_GsqT3qDJjYz_ijy0g
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sjn": "https://us06web.zoom.us/meeting/register/5-jrs4mPSyezTFfrCwoPdw?mc_cid=9d4c8b8c83&mc_eid=f6b9d64e2d#/registration"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sjn
SUMMARY:Find Your People: Engagement Strategies for Bringing Solutions Rep
 orting to the Community
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T000000
UID:d3094fd055ff60c4c482785c44bb6ec8@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Online\nThere is sometimes a gulf in reporting: Whether due to
  trust or access\, the people most in need of the information can struggle
  to obtain it. SomeAdvancing Democracy granteeshave been addressing that i
 n creative ways. You can learn from them at “Find your people: Engagemen
 t strategies for bringing solutions reporting to the community.”\nWe’v
 e got two sessions\, May 7 and May 21\, each featuring two different newsr
 ooms finding success with including the public in solutions journalism. An
 d we’ll help you build your own road map for meaningful engagement — n
 ot just adding to your reach\, but building real relationships. You can si
 gn up for one or both.\nPart one — May 7: Gulf States Newsroom and Factc
 hequeado share how they embedded community listening into their solutions 
 reporting for the first time.\nPart two — May 21: Crosswinds News and Te
 xas Standard discuss building on prior solutions journalism training to de
 epen engagement on Native inclusion and adult education beats.
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://us06web.zoom.us/meeting/register/5-jrs4mPSyezTFfrCwoPdw?mc_cid
 =9d4c8b8c83&mc_eid=f6b9d64e2d#/registration
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
